            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at Dasushi - Danang Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Michel I\nHamburg, Germany10 contributions\n0\nTerrible restaurant!!!\nAug 2024 • Family\nIt's the worst restaurant I've ever seen. The entrance smells like the fried head of a ram from a nearby restaurant. It's terribly hot and stuffy, as the entire restaurant has one air conditioner. Staff barely speak English, had to use a Google translator. There are only 2 menus for the whole restaurant. The tuna sashimi was brought on a backing made of onions, which greatly spoiled its taste. The eel rolls were watered with a huge amount of sauce, which practically destroyed the taste of the eel. The oysters came without lemon and the oysters were very fat (Like double whites), per amateur. There was no water and gas. The only thing to note is that the staff tried very hard. \nI do not recommend this restaurant!!!\n\nI have never seen a worse restaurant. At the entrance there is a strong smell of fried ram's head from the neighboring restaurant. It is terribly hot and stuffy, since there is only one air conditioner for the entire restaurant. The staff barely speaks English, I had to use Google translator. There are only 2 menus for the entire restaurant. Tuna sashimi was brought on a bed of onions, which greatly spoiled its taste. Eel rolls were poured with a huge amount of sauce, which almost destroyed the taste of the eel. Oysters were brought without lemon and the oysters were very fatty (like double belons), an acquired taste. There was no sparkling water. The only thing that can be noted is that the staff tried very hard. I do not recommend this restaurant!!!\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten August 1, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
